// spec: LEX-032
//
// '#0' is not a Char.  A code point of 0 is refused where the program is read,
// exactly as an out-of-range one is [LEX-025].
//
// ⚠️ Only the LITERAL is refused.  [LEX-025] puts a Char at 0..10FFFF and the
// built-in Char(0) stays legal -- which it must, because the scanner's own
// end-of-input sentinel is Char(0), and a scanner that cannot name its
// sentinel cannot scan.  Str(Char(0)) still truncates a String, which is the
// half of DEF-08 that remains.

WriteLn (#0 is Char);
